       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. A confirmation alone doesn't change my concern. 50 mg once daily is five times the maximum labeled dose, and I know of no indication that calls for it. Repeated daily, it could cause severe hypotension and shock that would be hard to reverse. I'm not willing to place an order that could seriously harm the patient on that basis.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Amlodipine 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily\n- Amlodipine 10 mg once daily plus a second agent, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide-like diuretic, if the goal is stronger blood pressure control\n- A different dose you specify within the labeled range\n\nIf you believe there's a real reason for a supratherapeutic dose, such as a protocol or a specialist recommendation, the safer route is to discuss it with pharmacy and enter it through your institution's high-alert or override process. That way a second clinician reviews it."
      }
